\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  Raises Bar For Staff's In-Office Attendance\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katherine Hamilton \par \uc2 315 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is requiring its corporate workers to come in the office a minimum of four days a week, up from three, as the coffee chain pushes ahead on its turnaround plan.\par \par \uc2 The four-day requirement will begin in the new fiscal year, which starts in October, Chief Executive \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2  said Monday.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the new in-office requirement, leaders and people managers from \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's Support Center who are working remotely will have to relocate to Seattle or Toronto within 12 months. In February, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  asked its vice presidents who were working remotely to relocate to the two cities.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is offering a one-time voluntary-exit program with a cash payment for employees who don't want to comply with the new requirements.\par \par \uc2 The move is part of Niccol's cost-saving turnaround plan called Back to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . In February, the company laid off 1,100 corporate workers.\par \par \uc2 "We understand not everyone will agree with this approach," Niccol said. "But as a company built on human connection, and given the scale of the turnaround ahead, we believe this is the right path for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Niccol has a stipulation in his signing bonus with the coffee giant allowing him to live in Southern California and commute to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's headquarters on a corporate jet. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said Monday that Niccol has an office and residence in Seattle.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's new requirement follows other corporations that have limited hybrid-work options this year.\par \par \uc2 Some have received immediate backlash.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  shut down comments on an internal webpage after the bank's return-to-office policy, implemented in March, stirred criticism and suggestions of unionization among employees. \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 's corporate employees returned to the office full time in January, but the e-commerce retailer didn't have enough desks and parking for them.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250715el7f00008\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
