\par\par \b \uc2 Angeles Equity\uc2 , Kain Merge Occupational Health Companies\b0\par\par\uc2 By Laura Kreutzer \par \uc2 570 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 July 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lower midmarket private-equity firms \uc2 Angeles Equity Partners\uc2  and Kain Capital are combining two portfolio companies to create what the firms say will be one of the largest independent occupational healthcare providers in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Angeles Equity-backed Agile Occupational Medicine is merging with Kain-backed Akeso Occupational Health. Each firm will own a 50% stake in the combined operation, which will have 42 locations across California and Arizona, according to the firms. The combined business hasn't been given a name yet.\par \par \uc2 The operation provides services that include treatment of work-related injuries, pre-employment physical screenings, drug testing and other recurring employee testing requirements. As the industrial labor force ages and more manufacturing companies seek to bring their operations back to the U.S., demand is growing for occupational health providers, according to Tim Meyer, co-founder and managing partner at Los Angeles-based \uc2 Angeles Equity\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The labor pool becomes very tight and access to labor and the cost of labor becomes very difficult and very expensive" as reshoring accelerates, he said. The occupational health business aims to "help screen employees for new opportunities, but also get them back on the production line or factory floor as quickly as possible if there is an injury."\par \par \uc2 Angeles initially backed \uc2 Agile\uc2  in 2022, and later that year \uc2 Agile\uc2  acquired Pinnacle HealthCare in an add-on deal. \uc2 Agile\uc2  generated revenue of about $39.3 million in 2023, according to a California regulatory filing. Meanwhile, Akeso generated a bit more than $30 million in revenue during last year's first nine months, California records show.\par \par \uc2 Kain acquired Akeso in March 2020. The Covid pandemic initially slowed the company's expansion, according to Kunal Kain, managing partner of the New York-based firm.\par \par \uc2 "When Covid hit, a lot of school systems and other customers of ours were shut down, so we slowed acquisitions until we got out of it," Kain said. "Right around the time when \uc2 Agile\uc2  was launching and doing deals in Northern California, that's when we were expanding our footprint in Southern California."\par \par \uc2 The global occupational healthcare market was valued at nearly $5 billion in 2023 and is expected to grow to $7.45 billion by 2032, according to a report from market research and consulting firm SNS Insider.\par \par \uc2 But the market is highly fragmented -- populated by many small clinics -- which provides an advantage to companies that can build scale, according to Kain. The merger of \uc2 Agile\uc2  and Akeso gives the combined company significant heft across California, which has the fourth-largest economy in the world, with opportunities to expand its reach both there and in other states, he said.\par \par \uc2 In many areas, employers don't have access to occupational healthcare specialists, forcing them to send injured employees to emergency rooms for treatment, which tends to be expensive, said Kain.\par \par \uc2 "As we expand, we are increasing the competitiveness of the space," he said.\par \par \uc2 Adam Lerner, an operating partner at Angeles who worked on the deal, said he also sees opportunities for the combined company to offer more ancillary services, such as physical therapy, acupuncture or chiropractic care.\par \par \uc2 "Many of the injuries that come in require those types of services as part of their treatment protocol," Lerner said. Previously, "they've been referred out to other providers. We're looking to bring that in and be more of a one-stop shop."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250710el7a0000q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
