\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- \uc2 UPS\uc2  Offers Drivers Buyouts for First Time\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung \par \uc2 295 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B12\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  is offering buyouts to delivery drivers for the first time in its 117-year history. The company is seeking cost savings because of stagnant parcel volumes, rising labor costs and a long slump in the company's stock price.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  employs around 330,000 full- and part-time delivery drivers, clerks and package handlers represented by the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 . Full-time drivers are eligible for a buyout, the company said. \uc2 UPS\uc2  and the union declined to say how many full-time drivers \uc2 UPS\uc2  employs.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, \uc2 UPS\uc2  offered buyouts to its pilots and nearly 200 pilots took the offer.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  decided to offer buyouts to its drivers because the company is navigating "an unprecedented business landscape" and reorganizing its network, a company spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  drivers are among the highest-paid delivery drivers in the U.S. The average full-time driver will earn around $170,000 annually, including benefits, by the end of a five-year contract that \uc2 UPS\uc2  signed with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  in 2023. Many investors thought the company conceded too much ground to the union. \uc2 UPS\uc2  shares are down about 45% since July 24, 2023, the day before the company and the union reached their agreement.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  reported a 3.5% decline in the average daily package volume in the U.S. for the first quarter of this year, and has said it would deliver fewer packages for its largest customer, \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 , because they aren't profitable enough. In April, \uc2 UPS\uc2  said it would cut 20,000 operational jobs this year.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said the proposed buyout offers are far less than what rank-and-file members could make over the remainder of the current contract.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich445\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6675
