\par\par \b \uc2 Banks Turn to AI-Powered 'Digital Workers'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Isabelle Bousquette \par \uc2 654 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 July 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bank of New York Mellon\uc2  said it now employs dozens of artificial-intelligence-powered 'digital employees' that have company logins and work alongside its human staff.\par \par \uc2 Similar to human employees, these digital workers have direct managers they report to and work autonomously in areas like coding and payment instruction validation, said Chief Information Officer Leigh-Ann Russell. Soon they will have access to their own email accounts and may even be able to communicate with colleagues in other ways like through Microsoft Teams, she said.\par \par \uc2 "This is the next level," Russell said. While it is still early for the technology, Russell said, "I'm sure in six months' time it will become very, very prevalent."\par \par \uc2 What the bank, also known as BNY, calls "digital workers," other banks may refer to as "AI agents." And while the industry lacks a clear consensus on exact terminology, it is clear that the technology has a growing presence in financial services.\par \par \uc2 Others aren't necessarily taking the same approach of granting their AI full logins, but many say that they are shaping AI into applications that increasingly replicate the capabilities and workflows of human employees, taking on more and more tasks in areas like the software development life cycle and research. Several, like \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2 , say they are still figuring out the exact right access and management controls and system integrations and how humanlike these tech systems will become.\par \par \uc2 BNY said it took three months for its AI Hub to spin up two digital employee personas: one designed to clean up vulnerabilities in code and one designed to validate payment instructions. Each persona can exist in a few dozen instances, and each instance is assigned to work narrowly within a particular team, Russell said. That way no digital employee has broad access to information across the company, she added.\par \par \uc2 Because they have their own logins and can directly access the same apps as human employees, they can work autonomously, said Russell. For example, a digital engineer can log into company systems and see there is a vulnerability that needs to be patched, write the new code to patch it and then pass it on to a human manager for approval in the system.\par \par \uc2 BNY said it is aiming to grant its digital workforce access to more enterprise communication systems, such as email and Microsoft Teams, allowing them to proactively contact their human managers for issues they can't solve. It also is working to build digital employees that go beyond coding and payment instruction validation into other areas. The bank said it will continue to hire top human talent while also building out more digital employees.\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2 , Chief Analytics Officer Derek Waldron thinks of "digital employees" as more of a helpful model for business people to conceptualize AI tools. They are fundamentally different from human employees, of course, but also traditional software systems, and so they may need their own type of system connectivity and access management, he said. It is an open question exactly how much or how little access to give an agent, and it is going to have to be figured out on a case-by-case basis, he said.\par \par \uc2 And while it isn't yet clear exactly what it will look like, he does envision a future in which every employee will have an AI assistant and every client experience will have an AI concierge.\par \par \uc2 Scott Mullins, managing director, AWS for Financial Services, said the question of how to integrate digital workers with a human workforce is top of mind across the finance industry.\par \par \uc2 "How do we coordinate that work together?" he said. When it comes to digital workers, he added, "How do we manage those folks? How do we actually instruct those folks? What's the new operating model? Those are the answers that we're all working on right now."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250701el710001f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
