\par\par \b \uc2 New $30 Hourly Pay Vexes L.A. Hoteliers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kate King \par \uc2 955 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Hotel owners are in open revolt against Los Angeles's new $30-an-hour minimum wage, the latest blow to one of the country's poorest-performing lodging markets.\par \par \uc2 This was supposed to be a great time to own a hotel in L.A. The area will soon be at the center of the globe's premier sporting events, first as a host city for eight World Cup soccer games next year, and then the Super Bowl the following year. In 2028, L.A. hosts the Summer Olympic Games.\par \par \uc2 But a pullback in foreign visitors and other issues have caused the L.A. hotel business to stumble again this year.\par \par \uc2 Now, hotel owners have to contend with what local union leaders said will be the highest minimum wage in the country. The City Council voted last month to boost the wage for workers in hotels with 60 rooms or more. Hourly pay, currently $20.32, will increase every year until it reaches $30 in 2028.\par \par \uc2 The industry is mounting an effort to roll back the new minimum-wage law. Los Angeles hotel owners are petitioning to suspend the city's new ordinance, and several hotel owners have also threatened to pull out of agreements to provide blocks of rooms during the Olympic Games.\par \par \uc2 Some hoteliers said they were already eager to exit L.A., if only they could find an offramp. "We would love to sell" our L.A. hotels, said \uc2 Jon Bortz\uc2 , chief executive of \uc2 Pebblebrook Hotel Trust\uc2 , which owns two hotels in the city and seven more in the L.A. area. "But nobody will buy them."\par \par \uc2 Others said they are canceling renovation projects, closing or scaling back their hotels' restaurants and could eliminate valet parking because of the increased labor costs.\par \par \uc2 "The quality of the experience is going to go down," Bortz said. "And that's going to hurt tourism, and it's going to leave L.A. in sort of an embarrassing situation when it comes to the World Cup and the Olympics."\par \par \uc2 Now protests over federal immigration enforcement, which escalated when President Trump sent in the National Guard and U.S. Marines, are adding to the hotel market's uncertainty. Nationally, hospitality trade groups have lobbied the Trump administration for temporary visas for hotel workers as the industry grapples with workforce shortages. The administration said earlier this month that it would pause immigration arrests at hotels, farms and restaurants, though it later said workplace raids would continue.\par \par \uc2 L.A. already has one of the slowest recoveries from the Covid-19 pandemic among the U.S.'s top 25 hotel markets, according to real-estate data firm \uc2 CoStar Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The local hotel union, \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 11, drove the effort to increase the wage. Representing 32,000 hospitality and other workers in Southern California and Arizona, it is one of the most powerful unions in the lodging business.\par \par \uc2 Kurt Petersen, the union's co-president, said hotel owners can pay the higher wages, especially with next year's FIFA World Cup and \uc2 NBA\uc2  All-Star games, the Super Bowl and the Olympic Games all expected to juice room demand.\par \par \uc2 "Of course they can afford it," Petersen said. "Workers need to earn enough to be able to live in Los Angeles."\par \par \uc2 The median rental cost for a two-bedroom apartment in Los Angeles is $2,383 a month, 72% higher than the nationwide median rent, according to listing website \uc2 Apartment List\uc2 . The union is gathering signatures for a voter referendum to boost the wages of all L.A. workers.\par \par \uc2 The lodging industry said it was already facing serious headwinds, including a decline in international tourism after reports of foreign visitors being detained or deported from the U.S.\par \par \uc2 A shift by budget-conscious travelers to short-term rentals and a 3% increase in hotel inventory since 2019 have also hurt, said Michael Stathokostopoulos, senior director of Hospitality Analytics at \uc2 CoStar Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Even before the new minimum wage, the total average monthly cost of labor per occupied room this year at full-service hotels in the Los Angeles market had reached a record $250 as of April, Stathokostopoulos said. That is up 6% from a year earlier and is about 36% higher than the 2019 prepandemic benchmark of $184.\par \par \uc2 Hotel owners said they don't think the major sporting events will provide enough additional revenue to offset higher labor costs. The World Cup and Olympic Games will be held during Los Angeles's peak summer season and would therefore provide only an incremental bump, said Mark Beccaria, who owns the boutique Hotel Angeleno.\par \par \uc2 Beccaria said he is putting on hold a $10 million planned renovation of his hotel, in part because of the minimum-wage increase.\par \par \uc2 Pebblebrook\uc2  owns the W Los Angeles, not far from Rodeo Drive, and the Kimpton-branded Hotel Palomar. Both have been struggling with declining profitability since 2016.\par \par \uc2 Only these two of the company's hotels are in Los Angeles proper and will be required to pay the minimum-wage increase. But CEO Bortz said he would likely feel compelled to boost wages at his seven other properties in the broader Los Angeles market to stay competitive for labor.\par \par \uc2 In fact, wages are already set to rise in nearby Long Beach, where voters approved a new minimum of $29.50 by 2028.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Hotel & Lodging Association\uc2  is part of an effort to overturn the minimum-wage ordinance. If the opponents collect 93,000 signatures by the end of the month, the wage-increase's implementation will be paused for a year and the ordinance will go before Los Angeles voters in a referendum vote in June 2026.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw553\pich297\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8295\pichgoal4455
