\par\par \b \uc2 Companies Turn to Robots To Do the Heavy Lifting\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung \par \uc2 619 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The robots are coming for the last human warehouse jobs.\par \par \uc2 Loading and unloading a truck is backbreaking, mind-numbing work that retailers and parcel carriers have tried to solve for years. Workers may not stay long in these jobs. Summers and winters are particularly grueling for anyone stuck in a metal trailer, slinging heavy boxes. Injuries are common.\par \par \uc2 Automating this process has long been the holy grail of warehouse logistics. When loaded, packages must be fitted together to fill the available space and be sorted by weight -- with the heaviest items on the bottom -- so they don't topple or break. Unloading them is challenging, too, because the unloader must move in and out of a trailer, ferrying packages of different sizes and weights.\par \par \uc2 On a typical warehouse floor today, every task might be heavily automated -- except for workers loading and unloading the trucks. People who have worked these jobs say they have to stand for extended periods, hefting boxes as heavy as 70 pounds.\par \par \uc2 New advances in robotics are changing that.\par \par \uc2 Improved sensors and algorithms, advancements in AI and faster image-processing technology are making these robots proficient players in tasks that are like a game of 3-D Tetris.\par \par \uc2 Engineers at \uc2 Ambi Robotics\uc2  designed a videogame to train its robotic stacking system, AmbiStack. It simulated challenging situations, including heavy parcels and boxes with strange dimensions, said Jeff Mahler, \uc2 Ambi Robotics\uc2  co-founder and chief technology officer.\par \par \uc2 Another company, \uc2 Boston Dynamics\uc2 , has designed a robot called Stretch, named for its flexible arm that can reach the top corners of a trailer. With a vacuum gripper covered in suction cups, it can lift boxes weighing up to 50 pounds.\par \par \uc2 DHL\uc2  now has a total of seven Stretch robots in supply-chain facilities in three states and has trained nearly 100 associates to operate them. In Columbus, Ohio, one Stretch robot that \uc2 DHL\uc2  staff named "Johnny 5" unloads around 580 cases an hour, almost twice the rate of a human unloader.\par \par \uc2 DHL\uc2  in May signed an agreement with \uc2 Boston Dynamics\uc2  for 1,000 more robots. \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  is also increasing automation at its facilities, including for loading and unloading trailers -- a move that will help the company cut costs, UPS executives said in April. \uc2 FedEx\uc2  has been testing and refining the truck-loading process in one of its facilities with robotics company Dexterity since 2023. \uc2 Walmart\uc2  also has introduced robots that can unload a truck.\par \par \uc2 DHL\uc2  wanted a robot that had the flexibility to handle different products, that could move in and out of a trailer and that didn't require a large capital investment, said Sally Miller, global chief information officer of \uc2 DHL Supply Chain\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "These are hard jobs to fill, especially unloading a trailer in the warmer months," she said.\par \par \uc2 Stretch the Robot still has some difficulty picking up thin packages, and the robot can't unload bags yet. \uc2 Boston Dynamics\uc2  declined to say how much each robot costs but estimates that there is a two-year return on investment on the robots.\par \par \uc2 Megan Diveley, a warehouse worker at a logistics company in Virginia who has been loading trucks for around three years, said she got nasty bruises on her legs when she first started.\par \par \uc2 "It got better after I got stronger, but I am always peppered with bruises," said the 44-year-old.\par \par \uc2 Diveley said she fears losing her job and feels that worry even without the specter of robots. Lower volume, facility consolidation and cost-cutting at logistics companies are all factors that can result in layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Her advice for the humans still doing the job: stay hydrated and wear steel-toed shoes.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250624el6o00007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
