\par\par \uc2 Heard on the Street\par \b \uc2 The Real AI Message \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Is Sending to Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dan Gallagher \par \uc2 339 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B10\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 [Financial Analysis and Commentary]\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  chief \uc2 Andy Jassy\uc2  had a chilling message for employees this week: AI is coming for your jobs. But things at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  are more nuanced than that.\par \par \uc2 The company is unique among its big tech peers: \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's business model requires a huge number of warehouse workers and delivery drivers. The company reported 1.56 million full-time employees in its last quarterly filing -- nearly seven times the total of the next-largest megacap tech giant.\par \par \uc2 That equates to nearly $417,000 in annual revenue per \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employee. That is actually up 43% from three years ago, when \uc2 Amazon\uc2  was feeling the aftermath of its Covid-era hiring binge. But it is also the lowest of that efficiency measure of any tech company producing more than $100 billion in annual sales, according to data from \uc2 S&P Global Market Intelligence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 , \uc2 Apple\uc2 , \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2  parent \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  all generate $1 million to $3.6 million in annual revenue per employee. Getting to even the low end of that range would require \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to slash more than half of its total workforce at its current sales level.\par \par \uc2 That isn't going to happen. So Jassy's memo likely has another aim. More tech leaders are propagating the view that job security in the age of AI means learning to use it -- fast. "You're not going to lose your job to an AI, but you're going to lose your job to somebody who uses AI," \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  CEO \uc2 Jensen Huang\uc2  told the \uc2 Milken Institute\uc2  in late May.\par \par \uc2 Jassy echoed that belief in a memo to workers this week, imploring them to "be curious" about the technology. Those who do "will be well-positioned to have high impact and help us reinvent the company," he wrote.\par \par \uc2 By effectively threatening a pink slip to those who don't, Jassy at least guaranteed that the AI workshops at \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's offices will be humming.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw553\pich375\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal8295\pichgoal5625
