\par\par \uc2 Technology & Media\par \b \uc2 AI to Cut Size of Big Staff, Jassy Warns\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sebastian Herrera and Katherine Hamilton \par \uc2 307 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 , one of the largest U.S. employers, plans to reduce its workforce in the coming years because increasing use of artificial intelligence will eliminate the need for certain jobs.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Andy Jassy\uc2 , in a note to employees Tuesday, called generative artificial intelligence a once-in-a-lifetime technological change that is already altering how \uc2 Amazon\uc2  deals with consumers, other businesses and conducts its own operations.\par \par \uc2 He didn't specify how much the size of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's workforce would be reduced but said the efficiency gains from using generative artificial intelligence would result in cuts.\par \par \uc2 "As we roll out more Generative AI and agents, it should change the way our work is done," he said. "It's hard to know exactly where this nets out over time, but in the next few years, we expect that this will reduce our total corporate workforce."\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  doesn't expect to have mass layoffs in the near future like it did in 2022 and 2023, with the decrease in head count expected to happen largely through attrition, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 Yet some teams could see layoffs over time, the people said. Organizations such as teams working on the Alexa smart speaker have previously experienced layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Jassy's note was among the starkest commentaries to date from a major company on AI's likely impact on employment.\par \par \uc2 Firms ranging from retailersl to pharmaceuticals are using AI to perform an increasing number of functions. Executives say the technology promises to increase productivity, but it also can replace the need for certain workers, while creating demand for new kinds of roles.\par \par \uc2 About 41% of employers said they would downsize their workforce due to AI, a recent \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  survey found.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250618el6i00020\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
