\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: PwC to Revamp U.S. Advisory Business and Hire Thousands\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mark Maurer \par \uc2 711 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PricewaterhouseCoopers\uc2  is overhauling the structure of its U.S. advisory business and hiring for thousands of roles as it sees recovering demand for such services.\par \par \uc2 The firm told workers Tuesday it plans to expand its advisory divisions to eight from four to provide more industry-specific services to companies, effective July 1. It also will embed managed services -- in which consultants operate part of a client's business, such as information technology and human resources -- in each of the divisions as opposed to keeping that group separate.\par \par \uc2 PwC, one of the Big Four accounting firms, now has four advisory groups, which it refers to as platforms: deals; cyber, risk and regulation; technology and business modernization; and managed services.\par \par \uc2 Cyber, risk and regulation will become two groups: cyber privacy and tech risk, and overall risk and regulation.\par \par \uc2 The tech transformation group will be divided into five platforms: front-office consulting, such as on marketing and customer service; industry-specific strategy; supply chain; traditional finance and human resources; and cloud engineering and data analytics. The changes are aimed at responding to client demand for more specialized help, PwC said. Deals will keep the same name.\par \par \uc2 The eight platforms span the roughly 36,000 advisory partners and employees working for the U.S. unit, including about 15,000 people based in India. The firm said no layoffs are planned as part of the reorganization, and it is hiring for thousands of advisory roles, citing optimism around recovering demand for advisory services.\par \par \uc2 The reorganization is being "approached from a position of strength," said Tyson Cornell, PwC's U.S. advisory leader. "With the market rapidly changing, we are focused on how we evolve, concentrate our efforts, and utilize AI and technology to empower both our business and our clients."\par \par \uc2 The hiring and more positive consulting outlook comes after recent layoffs. PwC last fall underwent its first formal set of U.S. layoffs since 2009, cutting about 1,800 people, or roughly 2.5% of the U.S. workforce. The cuts centered on advisory and products and technology operations. In May, the firm slashed about 1,500 additional jobs, primarily in audit and tax. PwC and other large accounting firms also focus on individual performance as the basis for some cuts.\par \par \uc2 PwC said it hopes the new structure helps it boost consulting capabilities in areas like e-commerce, particularly when serving companies with which it has partnerships. The firm has joint business relationships with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , \uc2 Salesforce\uc2 , SAP and dozens of other companies.\par \par \uc2 PwC plans to install industry leaders to monitor trends across certain sectors, a higher-level role than its existing 10 sector leaders who are more focused on day-to-day business opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Advisory is PwC's largest of three business lines, ahead of audit and tax. PwC's global advisory revenue rose 3.1% for the year ended June 2024, the lowest rate of growth since 2020, as clients scaled back on certain professional services at the firm and others.\par \par \uc2 Managed services will no longer have its own profit-and-loss statement as a separate platform. Partners and employees in managed services will work more closely with one of the eight platforms, for example helping run financial planning or integrate digital technology into a business for a client, PwC said.\par \par \uc2 Tim Canonico, who oversees consulting on U.S. business outcomes within managed services, is set to succeed Nikki Parham as leader of managed services after she retires at the end of the month, PwC said.\par \par \uc2 The moves are part of a broader effort by U.S. leader Paul Griggs to improve the structure of the U.S. operation. A little over a year into the role, Griggs has restructured the products and technology teams to further embed them in individual business lines, streamlined processes in business services, and carried out two rounds of layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Griggs last year also shifted the U.S. unit back to three business lines from two. Tax returned to being a separate U.S. business last July. The firm in 2021 combined its tax-reporting and accounting businesses into one unit called trust solutions, with remaining revenue stemming from consulting solutions, which included tax consulting.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250611el6b00034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
