\par\par \b \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2  to Cut 7,000 Jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natasha Khan \par \uc2 288 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Procter & Gamble\uc2  said it would cut 7,000 jobs, or roughly 15% of its nonmanufacturing workforce around the world, over the next two years.\par \par \uc2 The maker of Tide detergent, Pampers diapers and Bounty paper towels had about 108,000 total employees as of June last year.\par \par \uc2 P&G\uc2  executives, speaking at a conference in Paris, also said they plan to trim the company's product portfolio, exiting some categories and divesting it of some smaller brands in certain markets. The company didn't offer specifics on those plans.\par \par \uc2 P&G\uc2  in April reported a decline in quarterly sales and lowered its fiscal-year sales forecast, citing consumer uncertainty and a volatile geopolitical environment. To mitigate the impact of tariffs, the company in April said it would consider cutting costs, changing product formulations and raising prices on some items. \uc2 P&G\uc2  also faces stiff competition in a battle for market share as shoppers tighten their belts.\par \par \uc2 Since President Trump started a global trade war, companies have been taking a close look at expenses, both to absorb some of the costs of tariffs and in anticipation of an economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 P&G\uc2  said its staff cuts are part of a reorganization intended to create a better work structure, with broader roles and smaller teams. The layoffs aren't for cost-cutting purposes, the company said.\par \par \uc2 The consumer giant over the past decade has scaled back the number of categories in which it competes, homing in on its biggest daily-use products.\par \par \uc2 Last year, for example, \uc2 P&G\uc2  sold its Vidal Sassoon hair care brand in China. The company also made divestments of smaller brands in Europe and Latin America in recent years.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich445\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6675
