\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  Reduces Tech Staff In China In Revamp\b0\par\par\uc2 By Fabiana Negrin Ochoa \par \uc2 270 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  will reduce its technology workforce in China by about 3,500 as part of a continuing restructuring to streamline global operations.\par \par \uc2 The job cuts affect technology staff based in Shanghai and Dalian who provide financial technology and operational services for \uc2 Citi\uc2 's businesses globally.\par \par \uc2 The bank disclosed the move on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Some roles will be eliminated, others will be moved, and the remaining employees will support \uc2 Citi\uc2 's businesses in China and Hong Kong, the bank said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The move won't affect its Citibank (China) Co. subsidiary in China, which houses the lender's core banking businesses. Shanghai, where the unit is based, remains an important location for \uc2 Citi\uc2 , it said.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Citi\uc2  has been in China for 123 years, and our franchise remains an important part of our global network and growth plans," said Marc Luet, \uc2 Citi\uc2 's Japan, Asia North and Australia cluster and banking head.\par \par \uc2 Luet confirmed that \uc2 Citi\uc2  is pressing ahead with its plan to set up a wholly owned securities and futures company in China.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. bank has been pushing to establish a Chinese brokerage business since 2021 as part of efforts to grow its presence in the country, but has encountered regulatory hurdles.\par \par \uc2 "We are committed to our corporate and institutional clients in China and supporting their cross-border banking needs, as well as clients across our international network who do business there," Luet said.\par \par \uc2 Citi\uc2  still has six desks supporting Chinese multinational corporations, which are based in New York, Singapore, Hong Kong, Frankfurt, London and Dubai.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250606el6600042\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
