\par\par \b \uc2 How Not to Hire a North Korean Spy --- Practical advice on how to avoid hiring infiltrators, from some who nearly did\b0\par\par\uc2 By James Rundle \par \uc2 884 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 June 2025\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 North Korean workers are securing jobs at some of the largest American companies by masquerading as others, and earning good money in the process.\par \par \uc2 What started a few years ago as an example of Pyongyang's creativity in evading sanctions has evolved into a multimillion-dollar scheme for the regime. These workers infiltrate U.S. businesses to take tech jobs that command six-figure salaries, often several at a time, and they are everywhere.\par \par \uc2 Brandon Wales, vice president of cybersecurity strategy at \uc2 SentinelOne\uc2 , put it bluntly.\par \par \uc2 "If a company thinks that they haven't been targeted, that probably means that they've already hired one. That just means you haven't found them yet," said Wales, who until August was the executive director of the \uc2 U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SentinelOne\uc2  said in April that it had received more than 1,000 applications for jobs from suspected North Korean infiltrators.\par \par \uc2 Here's how corporate security chiefs can sniff out suspected North Korean applicants, from people who have had to do it.\par \par \uc2 Available resources\par \par \uc2 Sector-specific groups such as information sharing and analysis centers, or ISACs, have lists of email addresses and other details associated with known impostors.\par \par \uc2 That's how Nicholas Percoco, chief security officer at cryptocurrency exchange Kraken, knew he was dealing with a North Korean applicant.\par \par \uc2 "Whenever we receive intelligence, we plug it into our systems and look for all the places that these things may exist. And we did get a hit," he said.\par \par \uc2 That led to days of stringing the scammer along, to watch how he operated.\par \par \uc2 Watch for red flags\par \par \uc2 North Korean pretenders often demonstrate common behaviors, such as never turning their webcams on during meetings. If they do, they have a background on.\par \par \uc2 Many provide a U.S. residence during the hiring process, and then say that they had to move during onboarding, asking for equipment to be shipped to a different state.\par \par \uc2 "It's tricky because most of us allow remote work, and a lot of the folks that are getting these jobs, I mean, they're interviewing pretty well," said Charles Carmakal, chief technology officer at \uc2 Mandiant\uc2 , the incident-response arm of \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 's \uc2 Google\uc2  Cloud.\par \par \uc2 "They are actually skilled in the areas that they are applying for jobs in," he said.\par \par \uc2 Human connection\par \par \uc2 While applicants might be technically adept, some things just can't be faked, said Kraken's Percoco. Once the exchange identified the North Korean applicant, security asked the company's human-resources department to advance the application to the interview stage, so they could learn more about his tactics.\par \par \uc2 For supposedly elite intelligence operatives, the results were disappointing. While the worker did well on the technical interview, a second videoconference meeting with Percoco and others took place around Halloween last year, and the worker seemed stumped by simple questions about trick-or-treaters.\par \par \uc2 "We asked what kind of candy he had, and he couldn't name any," Percoco said. A request for recommendations for burger joints in the worker's supposed area yielded nothing.\par \par \uc2 Snapchat\uc2  illusions\par \par \uc2 Even when workers appear on screen, they may be using filters from social-media platforms to alter or mask their appearance. Such illusions can be convincing, but are easily bypassed, \uc2 Mandiant\uc2 's Carmakal said.\par \par \uc2 Asking interviewees to wave their hands in front of their faces can make the filters glitch. That might not disrupt sophisticated deepfakes, but for candidates using consumer-grade technology, it's a quick giveaway.\par \par \uc2 Know their goals\par \par \uc2 Many North Korean workers are there primarily to collect a paycheck to funnel back to their government. But some have more nefarious intentions, such as installing malware and backdoors on company servers.\par \par \uc2 Carmakal said he has seen instances in which workers attempt to extort companies after they are fired, by threatening to post data if they aren't paid a bonus or their last month's salary, he said.\par \par \uc2 Wales, of \uc2 SentinelOne\uc2 , said that a more worrying concern is what North Korea might do with its army of IT infiltrators in the future.\par \par \uc2 "In the short term, this is part of the efforts by North Korea to bring in money. But it also pre-positions North Korea on networks of key companies around the world, and how they use that access down the road could be pretty significant," he said.\par \par \uc2 One example of a situation that could have spiraled out of control occurred at cybersecurity vendor \uc2 KnowBe4\uc2 , which detailed in October how it hired a North Korean worker, who immediately attempted to install malware on company devices.\par \par \uc2 The activity was detected, and the worker's access was shut down before he could finish.\par \par \uc2 At Kraken, which is fully remote, Percoco said there are layers of controls designed to detect red flags -- for instance, a user who is working from a different location than the one he or she claims to be located in.\par \par \uc2 Kraken is investing in artificial-intelligence technology to help detect deepfakes, he said.\par \par \uc2 The concerning aspect of the North Korean applicant, he said, was that initial checks failed.\par \par \uc2 "He actually passed our third-party background check, because he was using someone's real identity," Percoco said.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020250603el630000a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
